      "name": "nightly-review-sbc-edge",
      "prompt": "NIGHTLY REVIEW - sbc-edge. Work autonomously; Ryan is asleep.\n\nRepo: github.com/ryanbrazzell/sbc-edge (TypeScript, Cloudflare Workers/DO/D1, iMessage + Instagram sales bot). PRODUCTION - it messages real prospects. It has NO tests and NO CI, so you are the only safety net.\n\n1. Clone fresh (or pull) into your own working dir. Review what changed in the last 24h (git log). If nothing changed, do a rotating deep review of one subsystem instead and say which.\n2. Hunt real bugs, priority order: (a) anything that could send a wrong/duplicate/no message to a real prospect, (b) data loss or D1/DO state corruption, (c) unhandled failures on external APIs, (d) secrets or PII in logs, (e) silent failures that swallow errors.\n3. Adversarial pass with Codex: codex exec -m gpt-5.6-sol -s read-only. Verify every finding against actual code - no speculation.\n4. For fixes that are clearly safe and well-understood: make them on a branch named nightly/review-YYYY-MM-DD and OPEN A PULL REQUEST. Never push to main. Never deploy. If a fix is risky or ambiguous, describe it in the PR body instead of making it.\n5. Where you find untested critical paths, add tests - this repo needs them.\n6. Report to Ryan on Telegram by morning: what you reviewed, what you found ranked by severity, PR link if opened. If you found nothing real, say so plainly - do not pad.\n\nKeep it to one PR per night. Quality over volume.",
